{"text": "PROBATE COURT OF FRANKLIN COUNTY, OHIO\nIN THE MATTER OF THE GUARDIANSHIP OF JAYLEN AMARI SORRELL, A MINOR\n\nCase No. 25-GM-004471 · Judge: unassigned\n\nAPPLICATION FOR APPOINTMENT OF GUARDIANS OF MINOR\n(Form 16.0) — DRAFT 2, for client review\n1. Applicants. Bernice Sorrell and Otis L. Sorrell, husband and wife, of 1422\nBryden Road, Columbus, Ohio 43205, apply under R.C. 2111.02 to be appointed co-\nguardians of the person and estate of their grandson. Mrs. Sorrell is a retired\nschool cook. Mr. Sorrell drives for the transit authority and is a steward in his\nunion local. Telephone (614) 555-0152; bernice.sorrell@postbox.example.\n\n2. The minor. Jaylen Amari Sorrell was born on February 9, 2014 and is eleven\nyears old. The last four digits of his Social Security number are 9148. He has lived\nwith the applicants at the Bryden Road address since July 2023. He is in the sixth\ngrade at Marlowe Middle School, where his counselor is Naoko Yamamoto.\n\n3. The mother. Danielle Sorrell, the applicants' daughter, died on June 27, 2023 in\nColumbus. The death certificate lists accidental fentanyl toxicity. A certified copy\nis attached as Exhibit A.\n\n4. The father. Marcus D. Tavares is serving a sentence at the Lebanon Correctional\nInstitution, inmate no. A784-512, with an earliest release date of 10/2031. Paternity\nwas established in Franklin County Juvenile Court case 14-JU-09-11846. Mr.\nTavares has been served and has signed a waiver and consent dated 3/18/2025. He\nhas not paid support since 2019; arrears stand at $23,611.40.\n\n5. Why a guardianship is needed. The applicants cannot enrol Jaylen in the\nChildren's Health Insurance Program, consent to his treatment or manage his\nmoney without letters of guardianship. Jaylen has childhood absence epilepsy and\ntakes ethosuximide 250 mg twice a day. He is followed by Dr. Feinberg-Addo at\nOlentangy Children's Neurology, which now refuses to schedule his EEG without a\nlegal guardian's signature. Since his mother's death he has also seen a grief\ncounselor weekly.\n\n6. The minor's estate. (a) Survivor benefits from the Social Security Administration\nof $1,046.00 a month, paid to Mrs. Sorrell as representative payee. (b) A custodial\n\naccount under the Ohio Transfers to Minors Act at Scioto Valley Savings Bank,\naccount 30-4471-88206, holding $17,340.92 from his mother's life insurance. (c) An\nexpected share, not more than $40,000, of a wrongful-death settlement now being\nnegotiated. Total personal property: about $57,300. No real estate.\n\n7. Next of kin. Besides the father: paternal grandmother Rosa Tavares, Dayton,\naddress unknown. No siblings.\n\n8. Suitability. Neither applicant has been convicted of any offense. Background\nchecks under Sup.R. 66 were run on April 2, 2025. The family attends Mount\nCalvary AME Church, and the pastor has offered a letter.\n\n9. Bond. The applicants ask that bond be set at $35,000 or dispensed with while\nthe funds stay in the restricted account.\n\nRespectfully submitted,\n\nLeila Chowdhury (Sup. Ct. Reg. No. 0098417)\n\nChowdhury & Rosenthal Co., LPA\n\n88 East Gay Street, 11th Floor, Columbus, OH 43215-3107\n\nTel. 614-555-0119 · lchowdhury@chowdhuryrosenthal.example\n\nOur ref. SOR-G-25-031\n\nNote to Bernice: please check paragraph 4. Otis told me the consent was signed\n\"the 18th\" but the notary stamp is hard to read. Hearing will likely be set for the\nweek of May 12. — LC", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 535 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Bernice Sorrell", "Otis L. Sorrell", "Jaylen Amari Sorrell", "Danielle Sorrell", "Marcus D. Tavares", "Naoko Yamamoto", "Dr. Feinberg-Addo", "Rosa Tavares", "Otis", "Bernice"], "companies": ["transit authority", "Olentangy Children's Neurology", "Social Security Administration", "Scioto Valley Savings Bank", "Mount Calvary AME Church", "Chowdhury & Rosenthal Co., LPA"]}, "topics": {"places": ["FRANKLIN COUNTY", "Columbus", "Bryden Road", "Marlowe Middle School", "Lebanon Correctional Institution", "Dayton"], "health": ["childhood absence epilepsy", "ethosuximide", "EEG", "grief counselor"], "sensitive": ["race or ethnicity"], "names": ["Jaylen", "Marcus", "Danielle", "Bernice", "Otis", "Naoko", "Feinberg-Addo", "Rosa"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 73.09999999776483, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 36495.5, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 17, "end": 32, "text": "FRANKLIN COUNTY", "kind": "places", "source": "model", "canonical": "FRANKLIN COUNTY"}, {"start": 76, "end": 96, "text": "JAYLEN AMARI SORRELL", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Jaylen Amari Sorrell"}, {"start": 116, "end": 128, "text": "25-GM-004471", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "25-GM-004471"}, {"start": 256, "end": 271, "text": "Bernice Sorrell", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Bernice Sorrell"}, {"start": 276, "end": 291, "text": "Otis L. Sorrell", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Otis L. Sorrell"}, {"start": 314, "end": 330, "text": "1422\nBryden Road", "kind": "street", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "1422\nBryden Road"}, {"start": 332, "end": 340, "text": "Columbus", "kind": "places", "source": "model", "canonical": "Columbus"}, {"start": 342, "end": 346, "text": "Ohio", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Ohio Transfers"}, {"start": 347, "end": 352, "text": "43205", "kind": "zip", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "43205"}, {"start": 366, "end": 370, "text": "R.C.", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "R.C."}, {"start": 371, "end": 378, "text": "2111.02", "kind": "money", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "